stems do what we intend them to do—is a solvable problem if prioritized, and that unconstrained development will inevitably lead to catastrophic systemic instability. If this assumption is proven wrong, and alignment is impossible, then the only rational path would be a complete halt to development rather than a reckless race. For now, watch for whether new systems are being subjected to independent, rigorous testing before release, or if they are being deployed into the public sphere while still in a state of experimental uncertainty.",
