r calls for 'safety' or 'slowing down,' look at who benefits from the delay—usually, it is the established giants who can afford the compliance costs that crush new competitors. You can advocate for your own future by demanding open access to these technologies and supporting economic policies, like direct wealth distribution, that decouple basic human survival from the ability to hold a traditional job. The moral hazard is not the arrival of artificial intelligence, but the refusal to adapt our social systems to a world where labor is no longer the primary measure of human worth.",
